  "behavior": [
    "Authenticated centered DG rectangles supply live half-extents. The host retains raise as metadata but does not use it to move blast depth.",
    "Source unit-quad transforms provide center and extents in camera space; analytic perspective ray/ellipsoid intersection determines the visible path before the scene surface. The atlas still controls shape, palette, phase and fade.",
    "Dense emissive response varies continuously with visible path length. Foreground geometry fully outside the volume blocks it. A surface crossing the volume leaves a partial plume.",
    "One existing scene-color/depth snapshot supplies a restrained material-modulated local light, gated by surface orientation and distance. No extra pass, copy or ray marching.",
    "Non-centered/invalid/camera allocations do not invent a radius. Missing source geometry uses conservative plane/orthographic volume handling; generic ordering offsets cannot punch an explosion through a wall."
  ],
